<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore's Terminal 3 construction at S$1.5 bln.</title>
<headline>Singapore's Terminal 3 construction at S$1.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore said on Monday that the construction of Changi Airport's terminal three and related facilities are estimated to cost about Singapore $1.5 billion.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the new terminal would have a handling capacity of 20 million passengers annually. This would bring total handling capacity for the airport to 64 million passengers yearly.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
